From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: preserve Baldur Gen5 suspend, wakeup and NCM behaviour
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Keep the pinned TB323FU runtime USB fixes on the unified tree for the
Lenovo Y700 Gen5 (baldur).

The Kaanapali USB GDSCs stay in retention across system suspend instead
of powering off, as the other SoCs using these domains already do.  This
is naturally SoC scoped: only gcc-kaanapali changes.

When dwc3 powers the core off in host mode for system suspend, xHCI is
told that its state is gone, so it resets the controller instead of
restoring stale registers.  The flag and its resume quirk only act on
lenovo,baldur; every other machine keeps its existing power_lost state.

Alt-mode and UCSI notifications run on the freezable workqueue on
baldur, so an unplug during s2idle is handled after the I2C bus and PHYs
are resumed.  Other machines keep the exact existing system workqueue.

Baldur's eUSB2 PHY arms the eD-/eD+ line and rising edge for remote
wakeup, drops any edge latched while the line was off, and disables the
line non-lazily.  The QUSB2 line selection and the old module-knob
setting are preserved; other machines take none of these branches.

f_ncm restarts its TX timer when eth_start_xmit() reports NETDEV_TX_BUSY,
so a half-filled NTB is not stranded until more traffic arrives.  skb
ownership is unchanged.

Merged from pinned tb323fu-linux patches 0036, 0059, 0060, 0061, 0062 and
0104.  The code is the original author's work, rebased onto these
preimages; the rebase adds no Signed-off-by.

---
 8 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)
---

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -2616,8 +2616,13 @@
 		if (!PMSG_IS_AUTO(msg) &&
 		    (!device_may_wakeup(dwc->dev) || dwc->needs_full_reinit)) {
 			dwc3_core_exit(dwc);
+			if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+				dwc->xhci_power_lost = 1;
 			break;
 		}
+
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+			dwc->xhci_power_lost = 0;
 
 		/* Let controller to suspend HSPHY before PHY driver suspends */
 		if (dwc->dis_u2_susphy_quirk ||
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
@@ -1141,6 +1141,8 @@
  * @usb3_lpm_capable: set if hadrware supports Link Power Management
  * @usb2_lpm_disable: set to disable usb2 lpm for host
  * @usb2_gadget_lpm_disable: set to disable usb2 lpm for gadget
+ * @xhci_power_lost: the core was powered off for system suspend in host
+ *	mode; xHCI must not try to restore its state on resume
  * @needs_full_reinit: set to indicate the core may lose power and need full
  *			initialization during system pm
  * @disable_scramble_quirk: set if we enable the disable scramble quirk
@@ -1400,6 +1402,7 @@
 	unsigned		usb3_lpm_capable:1;
 	unsigned		usb2_lpm_disable:1;
 	unsigned		usb2_gadget_lpm_disable:1;
+	unsigned		xhci_power_lost:1;
 	unsigned		needs_full_reinit:1;
 
 	unsigned		disable_scramble_quirk:1;
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -13,9 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/usb.h>
 #include <linux/usb/hcd.h>
 
-#include "../host/xhci-port.h"
-#include "../host/xhci-ext-caps.h"
-#include "../host/xhci-caps.h"
+#include "../host/xhci.h"
 #include "../host/xhci-plat.h"
 #include "core.h"
 
@@ -77,7 +75,21 @@
 	dwc3_enable_susphy(dwc, true);
 }
 
+/*
+ * dwc3_suspend_common() powers the core off in host mode when it may not wake
+ * the system: xHCI then has to reset instead of restoring its state.
+ */
+static int dwc3_xhci_resume_quirk(struct usb_hcd *hcd)
+{
+	struct dwc3 *dwc = dev_get_drvdata(hcd->self.controller->parent);
+
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+		hcd_to_xhci_priv(hcd)->power_lost = dwc->xhci_power_lost;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct xhci_plat_priv dwc3_xhci_plat_quirk = {
+	.resume_quirk = dwc3_xhci_resume_quirk,
 	.plat_start = dwc3_xhci_plat_start,
 };
 
